  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a binary string SSS of length NNN. Your task is to generate a new binary string TTT of the same length such that each corresponding character of TTT is different from the character at the same position in SSS.\n\nIn other words, for each position iii (0≤i&lt;N0 ≤ i &lt; N0≤i&lt;N), the following condition must hold Ti≠SiT_i ≠ S_iTi​=Si​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN — the length of SSS.\nThe next line contains the binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line a binary string TTT of length NNN, where Ti≠SiT_i ≠ S_iTi​=Si​ for all valid indices iii.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤101 \\leq N \\leq 101≤N≤10",
      "SSS is a binary string, i.e, contains only the characters 000 and 111.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1\n0\n1\n1\n3\n101\n4\n0011",
        "output": "1\n0\n010\n1100",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 444: T→[1100]T \\xrightarrow{} [1100]T​[1100], since T0≠S0T_0 \\neq S_0T0​=S0​, T1≠S1T_1 \\neq S_1T1​=S1​, T2≠S2T_2 \\neq S_2T2​=S2​ and T3≠S3T_3 \\neq S_3T3​=S3​, TTT is a valid output."
      }
    ]
  },
